WEBVTT

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.580
Where have I seen this scenery before?

00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:28.840
Mother...?

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:34.230
<i>Onii-chan...</i>

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:36.670
<i>Onii-chan.</i>

00:00:36.670 --> 00:00:38.430
Onii-chan!

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:43.970
W-W-What!?

00:00:43.970 --> 00:00:45.400
A n-nightly visit!?

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:46.720
A nightly visit?

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:48.110
What are you talking about?

00:00:48.110 --> 00:00:49.710
It's already morning.

00:00:51.970 --> 00:00:54.180
I took the trouble to come and wake you.

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:55.940
What's with that reaction?

00:00:56.940 --> 00:01:00.150
If you're going to wake me up, do it with a sweet kiss!

00:01:00.150 --> 00:01:01.980
That's my intention, of course.

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:05.460
Just. Kidding.

00:01:06.790 --> 00:01:08.750
Breakfast is ready, okay?

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:14.470
Damn...

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:19.200
Things are a bit back to normal, I guess.

00:01:20.910 --> 00:01:23.170
Right, Mother?

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:39.160
tomodachi ni mo ienakatta

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:44.490
omoi wo tojikometa mama no

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:49.580
kokoro no naka mahou no furuutsu

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:54.550
tabereba tsutawaru... nante ne

00:01:55.800 --> 00:02:00.160
kyoushitsu de matteita no, mada

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:05.160
guuzen da to iiwake shiteru

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:10.750
sono egao wa tabun dareka no mono

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:16.210
yume ga watashi no negai wo kanaeru nara

00:02:16.210 --> 00:02:21.160
sotto agetai purezento yo

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:26.330
anata no niji shiawase ni todoku

00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:31.290
hashi e to kaeru wa te wo futte ne

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:36.570
ii no ii no

00:02:36.570 --> 00:02:41.920
mitsumeteitai dake nano...

00:02:54.020 --> 00:03:01.110
<i>Appearances</i>

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:00.420
Hey, Onii-chan.

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:02.460
Are you free this afternoon?

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:05.120
I don't have plans.

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:09.510
Then can you accompany me to the record shop?

00:03:09.510 --> 00:03:11.030
There's a CD I want.

00:03:11.030 --> 00:03:12.640
A CD?

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:17.840
Oh, right! The new album of the gods of punk, the Moon Pistons, comes out today!

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:20.350
Did I say I wanted to listen to that stuff?

00:03:20.350 --> 00:03:22.840
You have no clue about a man's tastes.

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:24.660
I'm not a man, am I?

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:28.970
How cute!

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:35.020
Did you make up with Riko-chan?

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:38.350
Dunno if we really "made up"...

00:03:38.350 --> 00:03:41.780
At least the atmosphere is back to normal.

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:45.290
But didn't Riko-chan...

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:47.260
You knew about that?

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:50.360
Umm... I...

00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:52.210
Yes... a bit...

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:55.710
Well, that's completely behind us now.

00:03:56.330 --> 00:03:58.710
So... are you okay with that?

00:03:59.270 --> 00:04:00.710
What are you talking about?

00:04:00.710 --> 00:04:03.280
No, it's nothing!

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:05.630
C'mon, let's hurry!

00:04:05.630 --> 00:04:06.720
We'll be late!

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:16.290
Konosaka-san!

00:04:18.550 --> 00:04:19.820
Sempai!

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:21.940
Did you think about our proposal?

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:25.390
I'm sure you can do it.

00:04:25.390 --> 00:04:26.780
So, please!

00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:28.390
I...

00:04:28.390 --> 00:04:29.960
...think it's impossible for me.

00:04:29.960 --> 00:04:31.900
Of course it's not!

00:04:34.410 --> 00:04:36.540
I can't do it after all.

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:37.960
I'm sorry!

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:44.560
What are we going to do...

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:46.450
What was that about?

00:04:46.450 --> 00:04:52.130
We wanted to ask Konosaka-san to play the piano at the next recital of the music club...

00:04:52.130 --> 00:04:53.180
Wow!

00:04:53.180 --> 00:04:55.300
Kirino-chan is really skilled at playing piano!

00:04:55.300 --> 00:04:56.690
I think it'd be great!

00:04:56.690 --> 00:04:57.930
Yes, but...

00:04:57.930 --> 00:04:59.210
You know...

00:04:59.210 --> 00:05:01.240
You think it's that?

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:02.820
What's "that"?

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:06.200
Konosaka-san is really great during practice as well...

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:08.910
...but she's never played the piece till the end.

00:05:27.540 --> 00:05:29.220
Onii-chan, let's hurry!

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:31.640
Right, we can't afford to find them sold out!

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:34.350
So you made up?

00:05:34.350 --> 00:05:36.550
What's that all of a sudden?

00:05:36.550 --> 00:05:40.770
There appeared to be some unrest between the two of you.

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:42.860
As if you were avoiding each other.

00:05:44.290 --> 00:05:46.970
Did something happen during that Gift incident?

00:05:46.970 --> 00:05:48.440
Not really.

00:05:48.440 --> 00:05:53.290
In that case, the grand scheme I devised at the beach had success?

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:55.690
It was difficult, you know.

00:05:56.140 --> 00:06:00.670
I even had to cooperate with a witch using fake Gifts against my will.

00:06:00.670 --> 00:06:02.700
You bastard, that freakshow was your doing!?

00:06:02.700 --> 00:06:04.920
Who cares, Onii-chan.

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:07.590
Let's hurry before the bread is sold out!

00:06:07.590 --> 00:06:09.180
Don't push me!

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:11.550
I get it, I get it!

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:17.340
Damn, that bastard Maki...

00:06:17.340 --> 00:06:18.700
Don't get so worked up.

00:06:18.700 --> 00:06:19.690
But...

00:06:19.690 --> 00:06:21.980
Well, what he said wasn't necessarily...

00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:26.110
What?

00:06:27.690 --> 00:06:29.130
Never mind.

00:06:29.130 --> 00:06:30.330
Weirdo.

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:33.850
Have we been fighting?

00:06:33.850 --> 00:06:35.410
Guess so.

00:06:35.410 --> 00:06:36.620
Let's forget about it.

00:06:37.100 --> 00:06:38.550
Hey, Onii-chan...

00:06:39.240 --> 00:06:40.750
I...

00:06:45.700 --> 00:06:48.570
Come to think of it, about Kirino...

00:06:49.220 --> 00:06:53.230
About her never finishing a piano piece...

00:06:53.230 --> 00:06:54.690
Why do you think that is?

00:06:54.690 --> 00:06:55.470
Dunno...

00:06:55.470 --> 00:06:57.500
I don't remember very well...

00:06:57.500 --> 00:07:01.360
...but she's done recitals when she was younger, right?

00:07:02.350 --> 00:07:04.850
Well, there's no need to pressure her.

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:11.780
I see...

00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:13.740
So they made up...

00:07:19.180 --> 00:07:20.250
Good day.

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:24.720
What are you doing here?

00:07:24.720 --> 00:07:27.460
I was lured by a sad piano tune.

00:07:29.160 --> 00:07:30.510
Just kidding!

00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:32.330
Is something troubling you?

00:07:32.330 --> 00:07:34.990
If you want, I can help you out.

00:07:34.990 --> 00:07:37.760
No... I don't really have any troubles...

00:07:39.970 --> 00:07:41.480
Is this...?

00:07:45.730 --> 00:07:46.920
Kirinon, if you...

00:07:46.920 --> 00:07:50.680
I mean, Kirino-chan, if you're really troubled by something...

00:07:50.680 --> 00:07:52.900
...this will be able to help you out.

00:07:55.210 --> 00:07:56.840
What will you wish for?

00:07:59.690 --> 00:08:01.590
Look, over there!

00:08:01.590 --> 00:08:02.460
A plane?

00:08:03.370 --> 00:08:05.140
It's that witch?

00:08:05.140 --> 00:08:06.460
What did she come here for?

00:08:06.930 --> 00:08:09.540
If the rumors are true, she came to give a Gift.

00:08:09.540 --> 00:08:10.820
A Gift?

00:08:10.820 --> 00:08:13.640
Every person living in this town has only one of those.

00:08:13.640 --> 00:08:16.260
And they can only use it once in their lifetime.

00:08:16.260 --> 00:08:18.220
How can she just distribute them to others?

00:08:18.220 --> 00:08:20.670
Everyone calls them "fake Gifts."

00:08:20.670 --> 00:08:22.190
Fake Gifts?

00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:25.140
She can use them as often as she wants.

00:08:25.140 --> 00:08:26.610
Who is she kidding?

00:08:27.060 --> 00:08:29.440
Gift isn't anything like that!

00:08:42.080 --> 00:08:43.830
<i>Narasaki Shopping District</i>

00:09:18.450 --> 00:09:20.030
Hey, Onii-chan.

00:09:20.030 --> 00:09:21.830
Wanna go check out the ocean?

00:09:21.830 --> 00:09:23.750
We can see it from here as well.

00:09:24.370 --> 00:09:26.800
That's not what I meant...

00:09:27.670 --> 00:09:29.250
Okay, okay.

00:09:33.360 --> 00:09:34.810
Feels so good!

00:09:34.810 --> 00:09:36.560
Onii-chan, come join me!

00:09:36.560 --> 00:09:37.870
I'll pass!

00:09:38.880 --> 00:09:40.510
You're so boring.

00:09:40.510 --> 00:09:43.790
Haven't you ever seen scenes like this in movies?

00:09:43.790 --> 00:09:46.020
Those are scenes between lovers, aren't they?

00:09:52.780 --> 00:09:55.150
It's nothing, never mind.

00:09:59.770 --> 00:10:01.160
Hey, Onii-chan.

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:02.290
What?

00:10:02.290 --> 00:10:04.070
About before.

00:10:04.070 --> 00:10:06.700
You know, when you confessed...

00:10:06.700 --> 00:10:07.930
About that.

00:10:07.930 --> 00:10:09.050
I know.

00:10:09.050 --> 00:10:10.360
Just forget about it.

00:10:10.360 --> 00:10:11.690
That's not what I mean...

00:10:12.590 --> 00:10:15.980
Can I... change the meaning of my answer?

00:10:16.750 --> 00:10:17.470
The meaning?

00:10:18.610 --> 00:10:20.970
The meaning of "I'm sorry."

00:10:22.720 --> 00:10:27.430
Can I change the meaning of "I'm sorry" to "I can't give you an answer right now"?

00:10:27.750 --> 00:10:28.730
Not right now?

00:10:33.560 --> 00:10:36.720
I can't say "yes" yet...

00:10:37.310 --> 00:10:39.820
But, it's not a "no" either.

00:10:39.820 --> 00:10:43.700
I'm... still your little sister, so...

00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:46.140
But at the same time... I...

00:10:46.140 --> 00:10:48.520
...is it... really that bad?

00:10:49.190 --> 00:10:50.160
The rainbow.

00:10:50.960 --> 00:10:52.370
Rainbows.

00:10:52.370 --> 00:10:54.810
I told you that Mother liked rainbows, didn't I?

00:10:55.390 --> 00:10:56.710
Why do you think that is?

00:10:57.770 --> 00:11:00.540
Chase after it all you want, you'll never catch up with it.

00:11:00.990 --> 00:11:02.730
But still, you feel like chasing it, don't you?

00:11:03.260 --> 00:11:04.920
That's what so nice about it.

00:11:05.370 --> 00:11:08.580
You want to catch up with it one day.

00:11:08.580 --> 00:11:10.470
But you'll never catch up.

00:11:10.470 --> 00:11:11.650
You'll catch up!

00:11:11.650 --> 00:11:12.980
One day, you will.

00:11:15.140 --> 00:11:16.480
That's what it's about.

00:11:24.060 --> 00:11:25.200
Riko?

00:11:26.090 --> 00:11:27.760
Wouldn't it be nice to catch up with it!

00:11:35.990 --> 00:11:37.120
Mother?

00:11:41.190 --> 00:11:42.380
Is something wrong?

00:11:45.110 --> 00:11:46.510
No, it's nothing!

00:11:46.510 --> 00:11:49.970
Let's go home, I'm getting hungry!

00:11:49.970 --> 00:11:50.920
Okay!

00:11:57.320 --> 00:11:59.280
I want to go back...

00:11:59.870 --> 00:12:01.160
...to those days...

00:12:15.430 --> 00:12:17.150
G'morning.

00:12:17.150 --> 00:12:18.750
Good morning, Onii-chan!

00:12:21.450 --> 00:12:22.790
Hey, Onii-chan.

00:12:23.470 --> 00:12:27.970
Would you like Japanese or French dressing on your salad?

00:12:30.980 --> 00:12:32.730
Onii-chan, what are you doing!?

00:12:37.550 --> 00:12:39.570
Are you still half asleep!?

00:12:41.740 --> 00:12:42.740
What?

00:12:43.620 --> 00:12:44.570
Err...

00:12:44.930 --> 00:12:50.140
If you keep rubbing me there, it might just get excited...

00:12:52.510 --> 00:12:53.410
Moron!

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:01.130
<i>Puberty</i>

00:13:05.070 --> 00:13:08.100
<i>Am I still sleeping...?</i>

00:13:13.160 --> 00:13:15.890
What on earth was that, this morning...

00:13:19.400 --> 00:13:21.360
That's right, at the beach...

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:32.060
Was it because of that?

00:13:32.060 --> 00:13:33.570
But why...

00:13:33.570 --> 00:13:34.930
Is something the matter?

00:13:36.170 --> 00:13:38.800
You're sighing while looking at Fukamine-san.

00:13:38.800 --> 00:13:40.730
Did you have a fight again?

00:13:40.730 --> 00:13:42.710
Nothing like that.

00:13:42.710 --> 00:13:44.880
I'm willing to give you advice.

00:13:45.340 --> 00:13:50.870
Is seeing a completely different person in someone else scientifically explainable?

00:13:50.870 --> 00:13:52.430
Let's see...

00:13:52.430 --> 00:13:54.110
It's either a striking resemblance...

00:13:54.110 --> 00:13:57.180
...or an abnormality has arisen in your brain.

00:13:57.180 --> 00:13:59.420
Don't say there's something wrong with my brain.

00:13:59.420 --> 00:14:00.590
Onii-chan?

00:14:03.290 --> 00:14:04.280
What's wrong?

00:14:04.280 --> 00:14:06.360
We have gym class next.

00:14:06.360 --> 00:14:08.610
You should hurry up and change.

00:14:09.570 --> 00:14:10.580
Riko, let's go!

00:14:10.580 --> 00:14:11.580
Yeah, let's hurry.

00:14:15.720 --> 00:14:18.250
Is Fukamine looking like a different person to you?

00:14:19.180 --> 00:14:20.450
Forget it.

00:14:32.830 --> 00:14:33.970
Watch out!

00:14:38.520 --> 00:14:39.880
You okay!?

00:14:40.680 --> 00:14:42.270
Are you okay, Onii-chan!?

00:14:43.930 --> 00:14:45.030
I'm fine.

00:14:46.380 --> 00:14:48.030
Onii-chan?

00:15:02.350 --> 00:15:03.540
Riko-chan.

00:15:04.380 --> 00:15:05.950
Where's Haruhiko-kun?

00:15:05.950 --> 00:15:09.130
He seems to have hurried back home.

00:15:09.130 --> 00:15:10.480
How odd.

00:15:10.480 --> 00:15:12.180
Did something happen?

00:15:12.180 --> 00:15:13.740
I'm not sure.

00:15:13.740 --> 00:15:16.730
He freaked out when he looked at me this morning as well.

00:15:16.730 --> 00:15:19.750
Like he'd just seen a ghost or something!

00:15:19.750 --> 00:15:21.060
Haruhiko-kun did?

00:15:21.060 --> 00:15:22.420
Why?

00:15:22.420 --> 00:15:24.820
Like I said, I have no clue.

00:15:25.720 --> 00:15:27.320
It couldn't be...

00:15:28.780 --> 00:15:31.640
You're seeing your mother in Riko-chan?

00:15:31.640 --> 00:15:32.750
Yeah.

00:15:32.750 --> 00:15:33.750
Why?

00:15:33.750 --> 00:15:35.450
How would I know?

00:15:35.450 --> 00:15:39.030
I've only seen my mother in a photo before.

00:15:39.030 --> 00:15:40.750
That's true...

00:15:40.750 --> 00:15:42.640
So then why...

00:15:42.640 --> 00:15:44.210
I have no clue.

00:15:44.210 --> 00:15:46.460
Maybe Riko-chan resembles her?

00:15:46.460 --> 00:15:47.840
Does she?

00:15:47.840 --> 00:15:50.610
I guess you can't really tell from just that photo...

00:15:51.830 --> 00:15:53.720
Oh... that's right!

00:15:58.630 --> 00:15:59.900
What is it?

00:15:59.900 --> 00:16:01.630
Photos!

00:16:01.630 --> 00:16:02.700
Photos?

00:16:02.700 --> 00:16:05.130
Your father told me to take care of them.

00:16:05.130 --> 00:16:09.100
He said he'd lose them if he left them in his messy house.

00:16:09.100 --> 00:16:09.740
Found 'em!

00:16:11.010 --> 00:16:12.150
Those couldn't be...

00:16:12.150 --> 00:16:15.680
I only skimmed through when I received them...

00:16:16.550 --> 00:16:17.890
She's the spitting image of her!

00:16:18.910 --> 00:16:20.260
Look at this!

00:16:20.790 --> 00:16:21.920
Riko!?

00:16:21.920 --> 00:16:25.590
No! That's Haru-san in her high school years!

00:16:25.590 --> 00:16:27.540
This is my mother?

00:16:28.150 --> 00:16:30.520
Surely, the uniform is different...

00:16:30.520 --> 00:16:31.610
But...

00:16:31.610 --> 00:16:33.530
She resembles Riko a lot, huh?

00:16:33.530 --> 00:16:35.850
I'm shocked as well!

00:16:36.610 --> 00:16:39.220
This can't be...

00:16:39.220 --> 00:16:43.080
It's no wonder you could mix up Riko-chan and Haru-san like this...

00:16:43.080 --> 00:16:46.620
But this is the first time I see these photos!

00:16:46.620 --> 00:16:48.230
How could I...

00:16:48.230 --> 00:16:51.710
You have a bit of a mother complex as well, right?

00:16:51.710 --> 00:16:57.690
Maybe you found the visage of the mother you always yearned for in Riko-chan!

00:16:57.690 --> 00:16:59.880
A sixth sense unrelated to the Gift.

00:16:59.880 --> 00:17:01.450
A miracle of love?

00:17:01.450 --> 00:17:03.160
How exciting!

00:17:04.070 --> 00:17:07.350
So... have you fallen in love with Riko-chan?

00:17:08.580 --> 00:17:09.810
No, no!

00:17:09.810 --> 00:17:11.580
Riko-chan is your little sister!

00:17:11.580 --> 00:17:15.030
If you're yearning for a mother, I'm always here for you!

00:17:15.030 --> 00:17:15.880
Okay?

00:17:15.880 --> 00:17:17.760
Don't be stupid!

00:17:18.460 --> 00:17:22.640
<i>Do I like Riko... because she resembles my mother?</i>

00:17:23.380 --> 00:17:25.250
<i>That can't be!</i>

00:17:40.140 --> 00:17:42.440
What is it? At least knock before you come in.

00:17:42.440 --> 00:17:43.570
I did!

00:17:43.570 --> 00:17:45.190
The music is too loud!

00:17:45.190 --> 00:17:46.600
So, what is it?

00:17:46.600 --> 00:17:47.790
The bath is ready.

00:17:47.790 --> 00:17:49.320
Okay.

00:17:50.810 --> 00:17:52.150
What is it?

00:17:52.150 --> 00:17:53.270
Get out.

00:17:54.050 --> 00:17:55.010
Just get out!

00:17:55.980 --> 00:17:57.320
What the...!?

00:17:57.320 --> 00:17:58.410
How rude!

00:18:00.400 --> 00:18:01.870
<i>If...</i>

00:18:01.870 --> 00:18:04.970
<i>...I'm really seeing my mother in Riko...</i>

00:18:05.690 --> 00:18:07.530
<i>If I like her because of that...</i>

00:18:11.870 --> 00:18:13.480
This is awful...

00:18:35.860 --> 00:18:36.840
Huh?

00:18:37.370 --> 00:18:38.830
You're alone?

00:18:38.830 --> 00:18:40.180
Where's Haruhiko-kun?

00:18:43.910 --> 00:18:46.530
He suddenly started avoiding me.

00:18:46.530 --> 00:18:48.600
I have no idea what's going on anymore.

00:18:49.750 --> 00:18:51.610
This is ticking me off!

00:18:51.610 --> 00:18:53.530
What the hell is his problem!?

00:19:00.610 --> 00:19:02.180
Haruhiko-kun!

00:19:08.170 --> 00:19:11.200
Sorry, but I want to go home on my own today.

00:19:12.600 --> 00:19:13.850
See you.

00:19:13.850 --> 00:19:14.590
Wait!

00:19:16.040 --> 00:19:20.260
Hey... has anything strange been happening around you?

00:19:21.430 --> 00:19:23.510
Like with Riko-chan...

00:19:23.930 --> 00:19:25.940
Why do you ask me that?

00:19:25.940 --> 00:19:27.030
Maybe...

00:19:27.030 --> 00:19:28.670
...just maybe...

00:19:28.670 --> 00:19:30.010
What?

00:19:30.010 --> 00:19:32.900
Well... to tell you the truth...

00:19:54.410 --> 00:19:55.830
A fake Gift?

00:19:55.830 --> 00:19:57.470
Above my house?

00:19:57.470 --> 00:19:58.840
Yes...

00:19:58.840 --> 00:20:01.660
So... what did you wish for?

00:20:01.660 --> 00:20:04.350
That's... umm...

00:20:06.810 --> 00:20:07.840
Kirino!

00:20:07.840 --> 00:20:09.690
No... nothing!

00:20:09.690 --> 00:20:15.940
I was only thinking how it'd be nice if we could be as close as we were in the past again!

00:20:15.940 --> 00:20:17.570
I'm telling the truth!

00:20:17.570 --> 00:20:18.970
As we were in the past?

00:20:19.680 --> 00:20:20.610
Because...

00:20:21.170 --> 00:20:25.200
...ever since Riko-chan came back, we've barely seen each other anymore.

00:20:26.280 --> 00:20:29.670
But I haven't wished for anything!

00:20:29.670 --> 00:20:30.920
I swear!

00:20:30.920 --> 00:20:32.000
In that case...

00:20:33.710 --> 00:20:37.600
...could it be that these "fake Gifts" interpret your words...

00:20:38.130 --> 00:20:40.970
...and act upon them without an explicit wish having been made?

00:20:40.970 --> 00:20:42.090
What?

00:20:42.090 --> 00:20:47.260
All I wanted during that courage test was to heat things up a bit.

00:20:47.260 --> 00:20:50.430
You didn't wish for that monster army?

00:20:50.430 --> 00:20:55.510
The fake Gift interpreted my words and spawned a monster army.

00:20:55.510 --> 00:20:57.070
That means...

00:20:57.070 --> 00:20:59.890
...it interpreted Kirino's words of its own accord?

00:21:00.520 --> 00:21:04.790
You said you saw a different person in Fukamine-san, didn't you?

00:21:04.790 --> 00:21:06.000
It couldn't be...!?

00:21:08.010 --> 00:21:09.380
I'm sorry!

00:21:09.380 --> 00:21:11.450
But... I...

00:21:11.450 --> 00:21:12.590
That's not it.

00:21:12.590 --> 00:21:16.300
You received the fake Gift from that witch, didn't you?

00:21:16.300 --> 00:21:17.080
Yes.

00:21:17.080 --> 00:21:19.440
Then we'll just have to find this witch.

00:21:19.440 --> 00:21:20.920
That is the only way.

00:21:20.920 --> 00:21:23.040
The fake Gifts are merely forgeries.

00:21:23.500 --> 00:21:25.970
The way to cancel its effect should be different from the original as well.

00:21:25.970 --> 00:21:27.090
All right!

00:21:29.560 --> 00:21:31.100
Oh boy...

00:21:31.100 --> 00:21:33.930
Does he even have any idea where to find the witch?

00:21:41.860 --> 00:21:43.320
<i>Maybe...</i>

00:21:43.320 --> 00:21:46.200
<i>...if everything that's happened was due to the fake Gift...</i>

00:21:47.510 --> 00:21:48.410
<i>If...</i>

00:21:48.900 --> 00:21:50.240
<i>...that is really so...</i>

00:21:55.300 --> 00:21:57.370
<i>Then that means I really do...!</i>

00:22:13.190 --> 00:22:17.370
kyoushitsu no sumikko de

00:22:18.260 --> 00:22:23.960
kuchizusanda okiniiri no uta

00:22:24.780 --> 00:22:29.890
naze ka kyou wa kanashii kimochi ga

00:22:30.930 --> 00:22:34.120
afureteshimatta yo

00:22:35.670 --> 00:22:41.160
okaeri, watashi  machi wa yasashiku

00:22:41.160 --> 00:22:44.950
mukaetekureru no

00:22:44.950 --> 00:22:49.140
nee anata ni aitai na

00:22:50.700 --> 00:22:56.260
umaku waraetenai toki wa sotto oshiete hoshii

00:22:56.260 --> 00:23:01.180
hikikaesenakunaru mae ni

00:23:02.250 --> 00:23:05.130
futari kokoroniji wo kakete

00:23:05.130 --> 00:23:07.940
hitori ja nai to itte ne

00:23:07.940 --> 00:23:14.080
inori ga todokimasu youni

00:23:31.860 --> 00:23:33.950
I was told...

00:23:33.950 --> 00:23:36.980
"Happiness is something that is easily attainable."

00:23:38.060 --> 00:23:39.490
But I'm thinking...

00:23:39.490 --> 00:23:42.780
...is happiness really something so easily attainable?

00:23:43.560 --> 00:23:45.020
Gift.

00:23:45.020 --> 00:23:47.050
The power to bring happiness to the people.

00:23:47.820 --> 00:23:52.700
Hey, Amami-kun. What exactly is happiness?

00:23:50.840 --> 00:24:01.010
<i>The Meaning of Happiness</i>

00:23:54.030 --> 00:23:55.960
Next time, "The Meaning of Happiness."

00:23:56.640 --> 00:23:59.410
Who will you give your Gift?
